                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Disclaimers and Dragons [/h1]\n\nThis game is super early access. If it were released as is, I doubt even high profile reviewers known for talking about the worst Unity3d asset flips on Steam would even touch it. This game feels like something my friends and I would have dreamed up in High School and it has the polish as such but where the game is now, we would've given up and done something else.\n\n[h1] So it's... Norse? [/h1]\n\nEh, not really. The story so far is straightforward: Odin told you go get the hammer of Thor so he can reuinite you with Freya. Aside from that, it looks like a bright sunny day in a mountainous region. Lizardmen, \"Orcs\", and giants abound, there's nothing that reads \"Norse\" in this.\n\n[h1] Well I got a few bucks to spend, what do you do in the game? [/h1]\n\nBefore you spend a few bucks, check yourself. All you're going to be doing is moving backwards and shooting fireballs. It's literally all there is to do. You have a selection of spells but there is no need to put yourself into danger when you can walk backwards and shoot fireballs.\n\n[h1] So... avoid the game? [/h1]\n\nAs of now, yes. If this developer is a new programmer and is learning things along the way, this game could end up being a really personal passion project for them and that in turn could end up being fun but part of the game right now is fun enough to consider a game. And the cost of 10 bucks (CAD) for 20 minutes of gameplay is far too expensive.",
